{
  "id": "5aec828105-radsimp-fix-a-fraction-bug-when-strict-t",
  "repo": "https://github.com/sympy/sympy.git",
  "commit": "8462653c96a68590102e13d30c7c541bc38c9019",
  "prompt": "fraction(expr, exact=True) is wrong for an unevaluated negative power: for u = Pow(2, -2, evaluate=False), fraction(u, exact=True) should be (1, Pow(2, 2, evaluate=False)), keeping the exponent unevaluated.\n\nFor example (with x, y, z, s, t from sympy.abc):\n\n```python\nfrom sympy import *\n\nfraction(Pow(2, -2, evaluate=False), exact=True)\n# currently: (1, 4)\n# expected:  (1, 2**2)\n```\n\nOther inputs with the same problem should be handled as well.",
  "hidden_tests": [
    "sympy/simplify/tests/test_radsimp.py::test_fraction"
  ],
  "test_patch": "diff --git a/sympy/simplify/tests/test_radsimp.py b/sympy/simplify/tests/test_radsimp.py\nindex 15b18c5199..06da3fedf3 100644\n--- a/sympy/simplify/tests/test_radsimp.py\n+++ b/sympy/simplify/tests/test_radsimp.py\n@@ -445,6 +445,9 @@ def test_fraction():\n     assert fraction(m, exact=True) == \\\n             (Mul(1, 1, evaluate=False), Mul(2, 2, 1, evaluate=False))\n \n+    u = Pow(2, -2, evaluate=False)\n+    assert fraction(u, exact=True) == (1, Pow(2, 2, evaluate=False))\n+\n \n def test_issue_5615():\n     aA, Re, a, b, D = symbols('aA Re a b D')\n",
